  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rehabilitation of short-cycle crops production to the food and nutritional security of vulnerable people affected by Hurricane Ian</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide food security assistance to communities affected by Hurricane Ian in western Cuba. This FAO project provides nutritive food through the provision of short cycle vegetables. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 129,758 people, including 38,161 women, 75,854 men, and 15,743 children.</narrative>
  </description>
